00:11:09.720 --> 00:11:11.790
to try to recoup your losses.

00:11:11.790 --> 00:11:14.717
It's dangerous because it
does have the potential

00:11:14.717 --> 00:11:16.953
to keep you chasing losses.

00:11:18.570 --> 00:11:19.511
Chasing losses

00:11:19.511 --> 00:11:22.983
is maybe the most dangerous
phrase in sports betting.

00:11:24.930 --> 00:11:26.970
I think there's an intuitive sense,

00:11:26.970 --> 00:11:28.410
if there are more things to bet on

00:11:28.410 --> 00:11:29.845
that creates more of an opportunity

00:11:29.845 --> 00:11:34.620
for someone who has a
compulsive behavior issue.

00:11:34.620 --> 00:11:35.683 position:66%
You look at the structural characteristics

00:11:35.683 --> 00:11:39.060 position:66%
of in-play betting, it is extremely rapid.

00:11:39.060 --> 00:11:41.700
While there's an illusion
of skill and control,

00:11:41.700 --> 00:11:44.643
actually, in many cases,
those bets are just,

00:11:45.600 --> 00:11:47.100
you know, it's almost like
playing a slot machine,

00:11:47.100 --> 00:11:49.440 position:64%
every five seconds you can bet a new one.

00:11:49.440 --> 00:11:50.760
Which can make betting on sports

00:11:50.760 --> 00:11:52.410
less about heightening the game,

00:11:52.410 --> 00:11:54.750
and more about about getting a fix.

00:11:54.750 --> 00:11:59.010
When you put sports betting
in a mobile or online form,

00:11:59.010 --> 00:12:01.710
it no longer is tied or pinned

00:12:01.710 --> 00:12:04.500
to the particular sport event.

00:12:04.500 --> 00:12:07.500
Not only can you play in-game

00:12:07.500 --> 00:12:10.530
on multiple things continuously,

00:12:10.530 --> 00:12:13.530 position:59%
you can also bet on after-game things.

00:12:13.530 --> 00:12:15.600 position:66%
You don't have to stop when the game ends.

00:12:15.600 --> 00:12:19.290
You're very hooked in and
confirmed in your behavior

00:12:19.290 --> 00:12:22.080 position:61%
because of this constant fast feedback.

00:12:22.080 --> 00:12:24.870
And while only 2% of
gamblers become addicted

00:12:24.870 --> 00:12:25.800
to gambling,

00:12:25.800 --> 00:12:29.760
for the ones who do, it has
the potential to ruin lives.

00:12:29.760 --> 00:12:32.040
The history of legalized
gambling in America

00:12:32.040 --> 00:12:36.420
has never been driven by
concerns about problem gambling.

00:12:36.420 --> 00:12:39.420
And so as we enter this
unprecedented wave,

00:12:39.420 --> 00:12:40.350
we're really concerned

00:12:40.350 --> 00:12:42.390 position:61%
about the increase in gambling problems

00:12:42.390 --> 00:12:45.186
that will accompany the
massive expansion of gambling.

00:12:48.120 --> 00:12:51.990 position:64%
Gambling really started to get bad for me

00:12:51.990 --> 00:12:54.033
when I was in college.

00:12:55.320 --> 00:12:57.540 position:59%
This is Joel Soper, a gambling addict,

00:12:57.540 --> 00:12:59.640 position:61%
and the author of 'Never Enough Zeros,'

00:12:59.640 --> 00:13:01.893
a book about his life as an addict.

00:13:02.820 --> 00:13:04.260
It got to the point

00:13:04.260 --> 00:13:08.100
where I owed a bunch
of different bookmakers

00:13:08.100 --> 00:13:10.440
over $1 million.

00:13:10.440 --> 00:13:12.446
Did you stop gambling after that?

00:13:12.446 --> 00:13:13.533
No.

00:13:17.550 --> 00:13:19.710
When they came out with these apps,

00:13:19.710 --> 00:13:21.930
they had all the proposition bets.

00:13:21.930 --> 00:13:23.700
They had the live betting.

00:13:23.700 --> 00:13:27.690 position:63%
So now I'm in action all day, every day.

00:13:27.690 --> 00:13:30.030
From the moment I get up,

00:13:30.030 --> 00:13:33.030 position:56%
I'm betting on international soccer,

00:13:33.030 --> 00:13:38.030
to the moment I go to bed,
I'm betting on Chinese tennis.

00:13:38.490 --> 00:13:40.860
With the help of a
gambling treatment program,

00:13:40.860 --> 00:13:43.890
Joel was eventually able to
kick his gambling addiction,

00:13:43.890 --> 00:13:46.530 position:58%
and is now devoted to helping others.

00:13:46.530 --> 00:13:48.875
'Cause of my experience

00:13:48.875 --> 00:13:52.350 position:64%
in the sports gambling world for so long,

00:13:52.350 --> 00:13:55.726
now I can share my
experience, strength, and hope

00:13:55.726 --> 00:14:00.300
to help other people caught
in the same addiction.

00:14:00.300 --> 00:14:01.800
I wanna educate people

00:14:01.800 --> 00:14:06.800
that are in positions to talk
to people about the risk,

00:14:06.810 --> 00:14:09.638 position:56%
the dangers of this sports gambling.

00:14:10.710 --> 00:14:11.760
Hey, it's Craig Carton-

00:14:11.760 --> 00:14:13.950 position:59%
While the risk for addiction is small,

00:14:13.950 --> 00:14:17.610
both DraftKings, FanDuel and
others say they are dedicated

00:14:17.610 --> 00:14:18.443 position:56%
to what's called responsible gaming.

00:14:18.443 --> 00:14:19.276
By and large in the United States,

00:14:22.230 --> 00:14:25.050
that responsibility is
primarily on the individual,

00:14:25.050 --> 00:14:28.560
but those who operate, profit
from, and regulate gambling

00:14:28.560 --> 00:14:31.830 position:64%
also have a role in responsible gambling.

00:14:31.830 --> 00:14:33.810 position:64%
Should always be a part of your playbook-

00:14:33.810 --> 00:14:34.643
Responsible gaming

00:14:34.643 --> 00:14:36.600
is something we wake up
every day thinking about.

00:14:36.600 --> 00:14:38.250 position:56%
It's a top priority of our business.

00:14:38.250 --> 00:14:41.850
The health and longevity of
the industry really depends

00:14:41.850 --> 00:14:44.340
on not just us, but
everyone getting this right.

00:14:44.340 --> 00:14:46.950 position:66%
I think that their economic future depends

00:14:46.950 --> 00:14:48.600
on responsible gambling.

00:14:48.600 --> 00:14:50.820 position:56%
The former employees I spoke to said

00:14:50.820 --> 00:14:53.700
that there was always
a company-wide message

00:14:53.700 --> 00:14:55.890 position:58%
that responsible gaming is important.

00:14:55.890 --> 00:14:57.300 position:59%
What I also heard from these employees

00:14:57.300 --> 00:15:00.060
was that most of these
responsible gaming measures

00:15:00.060 --> 00:15:02.076
are not proactive.

00:15:02.076 --> 00:15:04.800
They're typically reactive.

00:15:04.800 --> 00:15:06.182 position:59%
There's typically only an intervention

00:15:06.182 --> 00:15:08.040
after the damage has been done.

00:15:08.040 --> 00:15:09.600 position:64%
They're falling behind in their mortgage,

00:15:09.600 --> 00:15:11.312 position:61%
they've run up a huge credit card bill,

00:15:11.312 --> 00:15:13.503
they're feeling suicidal.

00:15:14.640 --> 00:15:15.473
For now,

00:15:15.473 --> 00:15:17.670 position:59%
the main requirement in many US states

00:15:17.670 --> 00:15:19.582 position:66%
is that companies provide helpline numbers

00:15:19.582 --> 00:15:21.077
and avoid marketing to people

00:15:21.077 --> 00:15:24.330 position:59%
on what's called self-exclusion lists.

00:15:24.330 --> 00:15:25.195
There are some companies

00:15:25.195 --> 00:15:27.847
that have done some innovative
things with their apps.

00:15:27.847 --> 00:15:30.450
You know, they collect
enormous amounts of data.

00:15:30.450 --> 00:15:31.990
They see how their users gamble.

00:15:31.990 --> 00:15:36.450
DraftKings and FanDuel
collect huge amounts of data

00:15:36.450 --> 00:15:37.620
on their customers,

00:15:37.620 --> 00:15:39.021 position:64%
and they're able to track their customers

00:15:39.021 --> 00:15:42.753
in ways that casino bosses
would've only dreamed of.

00:15:44.130 --> 00:15:46.350 position:64%
While that data is used for simple things

00:15:46.350 --> 00:15:48.960
like confirming customers'
age and location,

00:15:48.960 --> 00:15:51.450
it has other applications as well.

00:15:51.450 --> 00:15:54.840
These companies are not
simply gambling companies,

00:15:54.840 --> 00:15:56.520
they're technology companies,

00:15:56.520 --> 00:15:58.920
and they collect and
use data in the same way

00:15:58.920 --> 00:16:01.568
as other big technology companies.

00:16:01.568 --> 00:16:03.450
We're 100% a technology company.

00:16:03.450 --> 00:16:04.920 position:58%
That's the background that, you know,

00:16:04.920 --> 00:16:07.410 position:56%
myself and my co-founders come from.

00:16:07.410 --> 00:16:09.450 position:64%
We do obviously have a lot of information

00:16:09.450 --> 00:16:12.060 position:56%
about what users do on our platform,

00:16:12.060 --> 00:16:14.393
so what bets they make, what
sports they're interested in.

00:16:14.393 --> 00:16:18.003
We use that information to
help run our business better.

00:16:19.020 --> 00:16:20.075
As you use the app,

00:16:20.075 --> 00:16:22.770
you're tracked in ways
that we're familiar with

00:16:22.770 --> 00:16:25.320
from social media sites
and other internet sites.

00:16:25.320 --> 00:16:27.240
The companies have a good
idea of your net worth

00:16:27.240 --> 00:16:29.100
from the other websites you visit,

00:16:29.100 --> 00:16:30.723
from Google Analytics data.

00:16:31.890 --> 00:16:33.498 position:56%
State regulators allow the companies

00:16:33.498 --> 00:16:36.647
to profile customers based
on betting histories,

00:16:36.647 --> 00:16:40.740
and limit the size of some
wagers expected to win,

00:16:40.740 --> 00:16:43.037
much like traditional
casinos kicking out sharps

00:16:43.037 --> 00:16:45.690
from the blackjack table.

00:16:45.690 --> 00:16:48.510
Well, we limit customers
for a variety of reasons.

00:16:48.510 --> 00:16:50.575
Some of them are because we
have particular customers

00:16:50.575 --> 00:16:53.730
that we think take advantage
of certain weak lines,

00:16:53.730 --> 00:16:54.930
and things like that.

00:16:54.930 --> 00:16:56.520
Obviously we want people to win,

00:16:56.520 --> 00:16:58.170
that's an important
part of the experience,

00:16:58.170 --> 00:17:00.990
so we've never really shut off
a customer for that reason,

00:17:00.990 --> 00:17:03.723
but we also have to limit
our risk exposure too.

00:17:04.590 --> 00:17:06.930
Ultimately, by leaving
it up to the states,

00:17:06.930 --> 00:17:09.870
and with no federal
legislation on the horizon,

00:17:09.870 --> 00:17:11.356 position:61%
these organizations, for the most part,

00:17:11.356 --> 00:17:13.890
are left to police themselves.

00:17:13.890 --> 00:17:14.755
The vast majority of companies

00:17:14.755 --> 00:17:16.950
are taking these apps
and they're tuning them.

00:17:16.950 --> 00:17:18.910
They're turning up to 100

00:17:18.910 --> 00:17:21.210
in terms of maximizing revenue.

00:17:21.210 --> 00:17:24.420
They build in little or no
responsible gambling features.

00:17:24.420 --> 00:17:25.391 position:59%
The federal government is more focused

00:17:25.391 --> 00:17:29.580
on alcohol and opioids than
gambling at this point.

00:17:29.580 --> 00:17:31.713
The state level expansion
of sports betting

00:17:31.713 --> 00:17:33.875 position:66%
has been accompanied by a lot of lobbying,

00:17:33.875 --> 00:17:36.843 position:58%
but rarely has that lobbying included

00:17:36.843 --> 00:17:39.240 position:63%
strong, responsible gambling provisions,

00:17:39.240 --> 00:17:41.010
or problem gambling funding.

00:17:41.010 --> 00:17:43.977
The gaming industry
writ large loves to say

00:17:43.977 --> 00:17:48.977
there is no evidence, you
know, research-based evidence,

00:17:49.200 --> 00:17:53.160 position:56%
that points to any one intervention,

00:17:53.160 --> 00:17:55.597
or any one form of regulation.

00:17:55.597 --> 00:17:57.352
The main research that's been done

00:17:57.352 --> 00:17:59.520
is funded by the industry itself,

00:17:59.520 --> 00:18:02.820
and the industry prefers
to focus on research

00:18:02.820 --> 00:18:05.250 position:63%
that looks at individual responsibility,

00:18:05.250 --> 00:18:06.587 position:63%
rather than the potential responsibility

00:18:06.587 --> 00:18:09.570
of the industry in marketing,
you know, these products.

00:18:09.570 --> 00:18:12.434
Bill after bill that we've
seen introduced since 2018

00:18:12.434 --> 00:18:14.639 position:61%
has been very specific about tax rates,

00:18:14.639 --> 00:18:16.170
and number of licenses,

00:18:16.170 --> 00:18:18.186 position:64%
and every other aspect of sports betting,

00:18:18.186 --> 00:18:20.130
but somehow, curiously,

00:18:20.130 --> 00:18:22.481
problem gambling and responsible
gambling gets left out.

00:18:24.120 --> 00:18:25.830
While individuals ultimately bear

00:18:25.830 --> 00:18:28.080 position:64%
the responsibility for their own actions,

00:18:28.080 --> 00:18:30.267
many hope the biggest
companies in this area

00:18:30.267 --> 00:18:34.260
will make safety an ever
bigger part of their mandate,

00:18:34.260 --> 00:18:37.560
if only to assure this boom
doesn't end anytime soon.

00:18:37.560 --> 00:18:40.110
I think we can meet this moment.

00:18:40.110 --> 00:18:41.490 position:66%
I think it's gonna take a lotta hard work,

00:18:41.490 --> 00:18:44.160
it's gonna take a lot more
investment by the industry,

00:18:44.160 --> 00:18:45.499
but that's starting to come around.

